<http://data.silknow.org/object/0a15d4b6-049f-3065-bbb9-2f3ba20c7e95/observation/4>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "British Galleries:\nThe range of luxury furnishings used in wealthy households included embroidered carpets. They were not used on the floor but as decorative table covers. The colourful and lively borders on this carpet were intended to hang down around the edges of the table and to be clearly visible. The absence of heraldry suggests that it was made for sale on the open market rather than as a specific commission. [27/03/2003]"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/0a15d4b6-049f-3065-bbb9-2f3ba20c7e95> .

